From d9f98faf76a64bc5609ea134183dc8096041257f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yomathnotcool <125728853+DengZhiyuan-math@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:07:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: structure turns apart from the proof budget, under one
 Pursue total fixed at Start (#19)

A node's proof budget covers its Prover, Verifier, Typesetter and Numerics
turns and is a ceiling, not an allocation. Decomposer turns are structure:
per parent one first split and one re-split; a second re-split is refused
and noted. They spend none of the parent's proof turns.

Every real turn counts toward the Pursue's total and every run toward its
one time limit: a PursueBudget fixed at Start (the researcher's limits, or
pursue_limits' default: node budget x max(1, open nodes at Start) + the
structure allowance), shared by a project Pursue's Reader and each
Theorem's Coordinator, and never raised by retries, re-splits or new
Claims. A run's cap is what is left of its node budget and of the total
once the running runs' caps are set aside; AgentRun.start takes a minutes
cap the same way.

A failed launch (a run that ends before any turn) spends no turn; three in
a Start, the first attempt counted, and the node is not tried again, its
claim given back and the failure recorded apart. The end of each Start
notes real turns and failed launches separately. At the end of the total
or the time limit, a parent whose re-split was due is Interrupted, saying
the total prevented it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
